{"kind":"assert","text":"Additional open choice for the pending attention handoff clarification, without changing frozen Draft1 bytes. Current reads.ts principalsOf selects the member, its current teams and its current role; attentionItems filters those principals and pos greater than the supplied position. core.ts attendAdmins actually stores role:admin rows, and policy notification stores n.to as the principal. admission.ts set-role/team updates membership without reissuing those older queue rows in those branches. Thus a role/team change can make a previously unseen row visible at a position below the receiver's saved cursor. This is a source-derived visibility case, not a reproduced runtime failure or a claim that the Room's incremental API violates its contract.\n\nThe receiver design should explicitly decide how it obtains current open work when its principals or configured work filter change: a bounded fresh queue/current-state catch-up with the same per-item durable identities, or a reviewed narrower rule that identifies what is intentionally excluded. The ping still cannot replace the acknowledged cursor. Do not silently treat an ordinary incremental page as a complete snapshot of newly authorized work. This supplements the cursor/submission review and may require a Draft2 sentence and acceptance scenario; it adopts no wire schema or new authority, adds no implementation lane, and keeps the highest-priority overhead verdict first.","body":{"scope":"additional source-grounded open choice for pending attention handoff review; no runtime bug claim","source_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967"}}